Mark XVIII: diagnostics bundle + opt-in crash reporting

- jarvis diagnostics bundle [--include-conversations] [--out <file>]
  writes a zip locally: version/OS/Python, license TIER (never the key),
  a redacted settings dump, the tail of logs/app.log, and conversation
  METADATA (ids/titles/turns/started_at). Message bodies are excluded
  unless --include-conversations is passed - and even then every line
  goes through the redactor and the transcript is size-capped. License
  key material never enters the bundle. LITE feature; works before setup.
- diagnostics.py: redact_text scrubs license keys, API key shapes
  (sk-/ghp-/xoxp-/AIza/Bearer headers), and emails; log_line appends
  redacted, size-capped lines to logs/app.log (wired into the sentinel
  announcer, background update failures, crash reports, and bundle
  creation); write_crash_report writes a redacted local crash file.
- Crash reporting is strictly opt-in (diagnostics.crash_reports, default
  off): cli.main wraps the dispatch and on an unhandled exception either
  writes the local crash file + prints instructions (opt-in) or preserves
  the previous behavior exactly by re-raising (opt-out). Nothing is ever
  uploaded.
- config: additive DiagnosticsConfig section; schema stays v4; settings
  show/set cover diagnostics.crash_reports.
- Tests: redaction (keys, license, emails; ordinary content survives);
  bundle contents (members present, no key, no bodies by default,
  metadata included, bodies + redaction with --include-conversations);
  crash file + log redaction; flag persistence.
- Version 3.5.0.
